                                                <msName>Pentateuch</msName>
                                            </msIdentifier>
                                            <msContents>
                                                <summary xml:lang="en">Pentateuch</summary>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-9-item-1">
                                                    <locus from="1v" to="84"/>
                                                    <title>Genesis</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <incipit>
                                                        <quote xml:lang="ar">في الاول خلق الله السماء و الارض و كانت الارض غير منظورة و غير مستعدة و الظلمة فوق اللجة</quote>
                                                    </incipit>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-9-item-2">
                                                    <locus from="85v" to="154v"/>
                                                    <title>Exodus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-9-item-3">
                                                    <locus from="155v" to="205v"/>
                                                    <title>Leviticus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-9-item-4">
                                                    <locus from="206v" to="271v"/>
                                                    <title>Numbers</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-9-item-5">
                                                    <locus from="272v" to="328"/>
                                                    <title>Deuteronomy</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Translated from the Septuagint.</note>
                                                </msItem>
                                            </msContents>
                                            <physDesc>
                                                <ab type="codicological-definition">
                                                    <objectType style="codex">Single manuscript</objectType>
                                                </ab>
                                                <objectDesc>
                                                    <supportDesc>
                                                        <support>
                                                            <material>Paper</material>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Oriental paper

BnF EAD physical description (srcphys_9423ce0b957bdbfb587fbd): 13 lignes à la page. Surface écrite 170 × 135 mm. Cahiers numérotés en lettres arabes à 10 fol.Papier oriental.329 fol. (f. 329 v laissé en blanc). Folioté en chiffres coptes.Écriture orientale (Égypte). Texte en partie vocalisé. — Titres rubriqués.244 × 168 mm.Reliure du XVIIIe s., maroquin rouge. Tranches dorées.</note>
                                                        </support>
                                                        <extent>
                                                            <measure unit="folio">329 folios (f. 329v blank); foliated in Coptic numerals</measure>
                                                            <dimensions>
                                                                <height unit="mm">244</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">168</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </extent>
                                                    </supportDesc>
                                                    <layoutDesc>
                                                        <summary>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">13 lines per page. Gatherings numbered in Arabic letters, 10 folios per gathering.</note>
                                                        </summary>
                                                        <layout writtenLines="13" columns="1" xml:id="layout-1">
                                                            <dimensions type="written">
                                                                <height unit="mm">170</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">135</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </layout>
                                                    </layoutDesc>
                                                </objectDesc>
                                                <handDesc>
                                                    <summary xml:lang="en">Eastern Arabic hand, described as Egyptian. Text partly vocalized.</summary>
                                                </handDesc>
                                                <scriptDesc>
                                                    <scriptNote script="arabic">
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Legacy hand scope: major.</note>
                                                    </scriptNote>
                                                </scriptDesc>
                                                <decoDesc>
                                                    <decoNote>
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Rubricated titles.</note>
                                                    </decoNote>
                                                </decoDesc>
                                                <bindingDesc>
                                                    <binding>
                                                        <decoNote>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">18th-century red morocco binding; gilt edges.</note>
                                                        </decoNote>
                                                    </binding>
                                                </bindingDesc>
                                            </physDesc>
                                            <history>
                                                <summary>BnF EAD catalogue (srcphys_9423ce0b957bdbfb587fbd): Pentateuque. Date described in the BnF catalogue: 1284.</summary>
                                                <provenance>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Waqf deed and reading marks at f. 1; table of contents and reading marks at ff. 84v-85; reading marks at ff. 155 and 272; reading mark of Naṣr ibn Ǧirǧis at f. 205v; pen trials at f. 206; reading mark of Yuwākīm, bishop of Beirut, dated 7042 from Adam / 1534 at f. 329.</note>
                                                </provenance>
                                                <acquisition>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">From the Bibliothèque de l’Oratoire.</note>
                                                </acquisition>
                                                <origin>
                                                    <origDate calendar="#gregorian" when="1284">1284</origDate>
                                                    <p>Anonymous copy completed in Rabīʿ II AH 683 (f. 328), for Hibat Allāh (f. 328v).</p>
                                                </origin>
                                            </history>
